  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council (whole council, two wards), polled Monday 15 January 1923. The five Unionist candidates for East Ward were returned unopposed; the seven West Ward seats were contested by seven Labour and two Unionist candidates, and all seven Labour men were returned. No party labels are printed against the names; the reports describe them as the five Unionist candidates. Returned unopposed."
